sequenceDiagram
    participant Scheduler as Background Scheduler
    participant PingJob as GatePing Job
    participant GateReg as GateRegistry
    participant GateClient as GateClient
    participant GateFI as Remote Gate (eu-fi01)
    participant GateDE as Remote Gate (eu-de01)
    participant DB as PostgreSQL

    Scheduler->>+PingJob: triggerPingJob()

    PingJob->>+GateReg: enabled()
    GateReg->>+DB: SELECT * FROM gates WHERE status != 'DISABLED'
    DB-->>-GateReg: [eu-fi01{ONLINE}, eu-de01{ONLINE}, eu-lt01{OFFLINE}]
    GateReg-->>-PingJob: [eu-fi01, eu-de01, eu-lt01]

    par Ping all enabled gates (parallel)
        PingJob->>+GateClient: ping(eu-fi01)

        alt gate.isFast (HTTP endpoint)
            GateClient->>+GateFI: POST /services/fast (X-API-Key: eu-ee31)
            GateFI-->>-GateClient: 200 OK
        else eDelivery (AS4 SOAP)
            GateClient->>GateFI: AS4 SOAP ping
            GateFI-->>GateClient: AS4 SOAP pong
        end

        GateClient->>+GateReg: save(gate.copy(status=ONLINE))
        GateReg->>+DB: UPDATE gates SET status='ONLINE' WHERE id='eu-fi01'
        DB-->>-GateReg: OK
        GateReg-->>-GateClient: saved
        GateClient-->>-PingJob: OK (eu-fi01 ONLINE)

        PingJob->>+GateClient: ping(eu-de01)
        GateClient->>+GateDE: POST /services/fast (X-API-Key: eu-ee31)
        GateDE-->>-GateClient: 503 Service Unavailable
        GateClient->>+GateReg: save(gate.copy(status=OFFLINE))
        GateReg->>+DB: UPDATE gates SET status='OFFLINE' WHERE id='eu-de01'
        DB-->>-GateReg: OK
        GateReg-->>-GateClient: saved
        GateClient-->>-PingJob: ERROR (eu-de01 OFFLINE)
    end

    PingJob-->>-Scheduler: ping complete
    Note over Scheduler: eu-fi01: ONLINE, eu-de01: OFFLINE<br/>Next ping scheduled in 5 minutes
